abstract: >-
  Code and aggregate evidence for model-conditional decision stability and
  latent explanation ambiguity in neural heart-sound screening, including
  functional bounds, projection controls, feasible witnesses, and a controlled
  support-gap distillation study. Both distillation criteria failed; the
  repository does not assert clinical superiority.
keywords:
  - heart sounds
  - hidden semi-Markov models
  - explainability
  - functional bounds
  - knowledge distillation
